### Known Issues

#### lisp-draft.k
- Was timing out with complex expression "(A.((B.C).D))"
- Simplified to "(A.B)" which now works
- The draft version has more complex Atom constraints (firstChar, someOtherChars, FIRSTCHAR/OTHERCHAR sequences)
- Uses `-heapcegar-cvc5` for string solving

#### lisp.k vs lisp-draft.k
- lisp.k: Simple Atom (just text field), works fast
- lisp-draft.k: Complex Atom with character validation (FIRSTCHAR, OTHERCHAR sequences)
- The extra constraints make solving harder

### Inheritance/Subclass Propagation
- Implemented propagateInstancesToSubclasses() in HeapLayout
- When parent class (e.g., S_Exp) has N instances, subclasses (Atom, ListExp) get at least N too
- This allows subclass objects to be used where parent types are expected
- Currently causes SMT baseline mismatches (expected) but outcomes (SAT/UNSAT) are preserved

